{"v": 1, "key": "cu-cu08", "cards": [{"id": "u4.t.flagellate", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term mid\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">FLAG<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">el<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">late<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"flagellate\" data-audio=\"audio/flagellate.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: flagellate\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"flagellate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><ellipse cx=\"80\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"45\" ry=\"22\" class=\"f1 k\"/><path d=\"M125 60 Q140 40 155 60 Q168 78 185 58\" class=\"s\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">flagellum whips to move the cell<\/text><text x=\"160\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">flagellum<\/text><line x1=\"160.0\" y1=\"32.0\" x2=\"150.0\" y2=\"50.0\"/><polygon points=\"150.0,50.0 150.3,45.0 154.1,47.1\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"60\" r=\"5\" class=\"f4\"/><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A protist that moves with one or more whip-like tails.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>鞭毛虫<\/b>：靠一条或多条鞭状尾巴移动的原生生物。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">flagellum = whip.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">flagellum = 鞭子。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What does a flagellate use to move?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">A flagellum (or several).<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u4.t.euglena", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">eu<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">GLE<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">na<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"euglena\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: euglena\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u4-euglena.webp\" width=\"533\" height=\"800\" alt=\"A euglena under a microscope: green chloroplasts and a red eyespot near the front end.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">A euglena under a microscope: green chloroplasts and a red eyespot near the front end.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">显微镜下的眼虫：绿色的叶绿体，前端附近有一个红色眼点。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: Petr Knotek · <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0\" rel=\"license noopener\">CC BY 4.0<\/a> · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Euglena_splendens_451542507.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"euglena\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><ellipse cx=\"85\" cy=\"62\" rx=\"48\" ry=\"20\" class=\"f3 k\"/><path d=\"M132 62 Q146 42 160 62 Q172 80 188 60\" class=\"s\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"56\" r=\"3\" class=\"f4\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">eyespot<\/text><line x1=\"120.0\" y1=\"40.0\" x2=\"120.0\" y2=\"53.0\"/><polygon points=\"120.0,53.0 117.8,48.5 122.2,48.5\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><ellipse cx=\"60\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"8\" ry=\"4\" class=\"f3\"/><ellipse cx=\"80\" cy=\"68\" rx=\"8\" ry=\"4\" class=\"f3\"/><ellipse cx=\"95\" cy=\"56\" rx=\"8\" ry=\"4\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">chloroplasts<\/text><line x1=\"80.0\" y1=\"95.0\" x2=\"80.0\" y2=\"74.0\"/><polygon points=\"80.0,74.0 82.2,78.5 77.8,78.5\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A single-celled protist with chloroplasts and a flagellum. It can make food or eat.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>眼虫<\/b>：有叶绿体和鞭毛的单细胞原生生物，既能自制食物也能摄食。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Euglena = &quot;true eye&quot; (eu = true, glene = eyeball).<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">eu = 真，glene = 眼珠。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: How can a euglena get food?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">By photosynthesis, or by eating, depending on conditions.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u4.t.eyespot", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">EYE<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">spot<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"eyespot\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: eyespot\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u4-eyespot.webp\" width=\"533\" height=\"800\" alt=\"A euglena under a microscope. The small red dot near one end is its eyespot.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">A euglena under a microscope. The small red dot near one end is its eyespot.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">显微镜下的眼虫。靠近一端的小红点就是眼点。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: Petr Knotek · <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0\" rel=\"license noopener\">CC BY 4.0<\/a> · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Euglena_sociabilis_433143410.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"eyespot\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"55\" ry=\"28\" class=\"f3 k\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"55\" r=\"5\" class=\"f4 k\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">eyespot<\/text><line x1=\"140.0\" y1=\"32.0\" x2=\"140.0\" y2=\"49.0\"/><polygon points=\"140.0,49.0 137.8,44.5 142.2,44.5\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><line x1=\"40.0\" y1=\"20.0\" x2=\"80.0\" y2=\"40.0\"/><polygon points=\"80.0,40.0 75.0,39.9 76.9,36.0\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">light<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A light-sensing spot in a euglena that helps it swim toward light.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>眼点<\/b>：眼虫中感光的小点，帮助它游向光。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">An eyespot is a &quot;spot&quot; that senses light, not a real eye.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">眼点只感光，不是真眼睛。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What does an eyespot detect?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Light.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u4.t.contractile-vacuole", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term sm\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">con<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">TRAC<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tile<\/span> <span class=\"st\">VAC<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">u<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ole<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"contractile vacuole\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: contractile vacuole\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u4-contractile-vacuole.webp\" width=\"751\" height=\"738\" alt=\"A paramecium under a microscope. The two lines point to its star-shaped contractile vacuoles.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">A paramecium under a microscope. The two lines point to its star-shaped contractile vacuoles.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">显微镜下的草履虫。两条线指着它星形的伸缩泡。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: derivative work: Hämbörger (talk) Paramecium.jpg: User:Josh Grosse · <a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/\" rel=\"license noopener\">CC BY-SA 3.0<\/a> · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paramecium_contractile_vacuoles.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"contractile vacuole\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"62\" ry=\"24\" class=\"f1 k\"/><line x1=\"55\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"52\" y2=\"33\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"72\" y1=\"36\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"29\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"90\" y1=\"35\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"28\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"35\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"28\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"128\" y1=\"36\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"29\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"145\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"148\" y2=\"33\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"55\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"52\" y2=\"87\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"72\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"91\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"90\" y1=\"85\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"92\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"85\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"92\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"128\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"91\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"145\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"148\" y2=\"87\" class=\"\"/><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"60\" r=\"8\" class=\"f1 k\"/><line x1=\"100.0\" y1=\"54.0\" x2=\"100.0\" y2=\"36.0\"/><polygon points=\"100.0,36.0 102.2,40.5 97.8,40.5\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"8.163265306122447\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">pumps water out so the cell does not burst<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">An organelle that pumps excess water out of freshwater protists.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>伸缩泡<\/b>：把淡水原生生物体内多余的水排出的细胞器。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">contract = squeeze. It squeezes water out.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">contract = 收缩。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Why do freshwater protists need contractile vacuoles?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Water keeps entering by osmosis, and the vacuole pumps it out.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u4.t.food-vacuole", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term mid\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">FOOD<\/span> <span class=\"st\">VAC<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">u<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ole<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"food vacuole\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: food vacuole\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"food vacuole\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M70 60 Q60 35 85 38 Q95 20 110 35 Q135 30 130 55 Q150 65 125 78 Q120 98 100 88 Q80 100 75 80 Q50 85 70 60 Z\" class=\"f3 k\"/><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"58\" r=\"9\" class=\"f4\"/><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"70\" r=\"6\" class=\"f6 k\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">food vacuole: digestion happens inside<\/text><line x1=\"96.0\" y1=\"100.0\" x2=\"92.0\" y2=\"76.0\"/><polygon points=\"92.0,76.0 94.9,80.1 90.6,80.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A bubble inside a cell where engulfed food is digested.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>食物泡<\/b>：细胞里消化被吞入食物的小泡。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">vacuole = a small empty space.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">vacuole 即小空腔。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Where is food digested in an amoeba?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">In a food vacuole.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u4.t.phagocytosis", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term mid\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">phag<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">o<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">cy<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">TO<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">sis<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"phagocytosis\" data-audio=\"audio/phagocytosis.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: phagocytosis\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"phagocytosis\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"53.6\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Pseudopods<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"62.8\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">surround<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">food<\/text><line x1=\"59.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"73.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"73.0,60.0 68.5,62.2 68.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"74\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"46.7\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Food<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"57.9\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">enclosed<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"69.1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">in a<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"80.3\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">vacuole<\/text><line x1=\"127.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"141.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"141.0,60.0 136.5,62.2 136.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"142\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"52.3\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Enzymes<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"63.5\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">digest<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"74.7\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">it<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">When a cell wraps around a particle and takes it in, forming a vacuole.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>吞噬作用<\/b>：细胞包裹颗粒并将其吞入，形成一个泡。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">phago = eat, cyto = cell. Cell eating.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">phago = 吃，cyto = 细胞。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What does phagocytosis mean in simple words?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Cell eating.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u4.t.plankton", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">PLANK<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ton<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"plankton\" data-audio=\"audio/plankton.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: plankton\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u4-plankton.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"559\" alt=\"A drop of sea water under a microscope: many kinds of plankton (bar = 100 micrometres).\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">A drop of sea water under a microscope: many kinds of plankton (bar = 100 micrometres).<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">显微镜下的一滴海水：多种浮游生物（比例尺 = 100 微米）。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: Jay Nadeau, Chris Lindensmith, Jody W. Deming, Vicente I. Fernandez, and Roman Stocker. … · <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\" rel=\"license noopener\">CC BY-SA 4.0<\/a> · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marine_microplankton.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"plankton\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"30\" width=\"180\" height=\"70\" rx=\"4\" class=\"f1\"/><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"55\" r=\"3\" class=\"f3\"/><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"70\" r=\"3\" class=\"f6\"/><circle cx=\"105\" cy=\"50\" r=\"3\" class=\"f3\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"72\" r=\"3\" class=\"f6\"/><circle cx=\"165\" cy=\"58\" r=\"3\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">drifting life<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">Tiny organisms that drift in water instead of swimming against currents.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>浮游生物<\/b>：随水漂流、而不是逆流游动的微小生物。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">plankton = Greek for drifter.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">plankton 在希腊语里是「漂流者」。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Does plankton swim against the current?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">No. It drifts.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}], "quiz": [{"id": "cu.q.u4.t.flagellate", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A protist that moves with one or more whip-like tails.”<\/i>", "opts": ["endosymbiotic theory", "flagellate", "paramecium", "amoeba"], "a": 1, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>flagellate<\/b>: A protist that moves with one or more whip-like tails. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">鞭毛虫<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u4.t.euglena", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A single-celled protist with chloroplasts and a flagellum. It can make food or eat.”<\/i>", "opts": ["nucleus", "diatom", "euglena", "zooplankton"], "a": 2, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>euglena<\/b>: A single-celled protist with chloroplasts and a flagellum. It can make food or eat. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">眼虫<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u4.t.eyespot", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A light-sensing spot in a euglena that helps it swim toward light.”<\/i>", "opts": ["photosynthesis", "paramecium", "protist", "eyespot"], "a": 3, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>eyespot<\/b>: A light-sensing spot in a euglena that helps it swim toward light. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">眼点<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u4.t.contractile-vacuole", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“An organelle that pumps excess water out of freshwater protists.”<\/i>", "opts": ["contractile vacuole", "diatom", "flagellate", "organelle"], "a": 0, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>contractile vacuole<\/b>: An organelle that pumps excess water out of freshwater protists. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">伸缩泡<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u4.t.food-vacuole", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A bubble inside a cell where engulfed food is digested.”<\/i>", "opts": ["colonial organism", "food vacuole", "photosynthesis", "green algae"], "a": 1, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>food vacuole<\/b>: A bubble inside a cell where engulfed food is digested. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">食物泡<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u4.t.phagocytosis", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“When a cell wraps around a particle and takes it in, forming a vacuole.”<\/i>", "opts": ["photosynthesis", "colonial organism", "vector", "phagocytosis"], "a": 3, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>phagocytosis<\/b>: When a cell wraps around a particle and takes it in, forming a vacuole. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">吞噬作用<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u4.t.plankton", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“Tiny organisms that drift in water instead of swimming against currents.”<\/i>", "opts": ["pseudopod", "plankton", "phytoplankton", "dinoflagellate"], "a": 1, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>plankton<\/b>: Tiny organisms that drift in water instead of swimming against currents. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">浮游生物<\/span>", "whys": null}]}